meta {
  name: Create Write Request
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/write-requests
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "title": "Fix patient status",
    "description": "Correct a mis-set flag",
    "connectionId": "{{connectionId}}",
    "selectSql": "SELECT id, active FROM patients WHERE id = 42",
    "writeSql": "UPDATE patients SET active = true WHERE id = 42",
    "noTransaction": false
  }
}

docs {
  Submit a write request. The server classifies `writeSql` itself:

  - **Single DML** (one INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE) — send a `selectSql` verify SELECT; it previews the affected rows.
  - **Migration** (multiple statements or any DDL, PostgreSQL/SQL Server only) — `selectSql` is ignored; the whole script runs as one transaction and rolls back atomically on failure. Set `noTransaction: true` only when the script contains a statement that can't run in a transaction (e.g. CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY, VACUUM) — it then commits statement-by-statement with NO rollback.

  On DIRECT-policy envs an authorized author executes immediately; otherwise it goes PENDING for approval.

  Requires a valid Bearer JWT ({{token}}).
  Requires **write mode** to be enabled.
}
